# Build + generated artifacts (the recompiled substrate is ~hundreds of MB of emitted C)
build/
scratch/
generated/

# The recompiled substrate's INPUTS come from YOUR OWN disc and are never committed: the disc image
# and anything extracted from it are the copyright holder's, not this repo's.
#
# Kept NARROW on purpose. Everything extracted lands under scratch/ (already ignored above); the
# patterns here are the belt to that braces, for a file dropped in the repo root. Broad patterns
# (*.exe, *.bin) would also match ordinary PROSE naming those files in docs, which floods
# tools/go_public.py's "docs referencing gitignored items" check with false positives — and a gate
# that cries wolf is one people stop reading.
*.chd
.env
# NOT listed here, deliberately: `SLUS_010.40` / `SLUS_*.*`. They were, and go_public.py's check C
# ("docs referencing SENSITIVE gitignored items") turns every gitignore pattern into a search token —
# measured 2026-08-12: those two produce the tokens `SLUS_010.40` and `SLUS_`, which every doc in this
# repo names in prose, so the audit becomes a wall of false positives and a gate that cries wolf is one
# people stop reading. The extracted executable lands under scratch/, ignored above, which is where the
# tooling puts it; a copy dropped loose in the repo root is caught by review, not by a pattern that
# breaks the audit. Same tradeoff spyro's .gitignore documents.

# The framework. Not tracked: either a symlink to the workspace shared clone (local) or a
# private clone at psxport.pin (fresh machine). Managed by tools/psxport_sync.py.
/external/psxport
# The vendored decomp builds into its own tree; it is a REFERENCE, we never build it here, but a
# curious session might.
external/rood-reverse/build/
external/rood-reverse/disks/
external/rood-reverse/.venv/
*.log

# Per-checkout player video preferences. The framework F1 overlay writes this file on every change;
# it is runtime state, not a shipping input (path can be overridden with PSXPORT_SETTINGS).
/psxport_settings.ini

# Python bytecode — never committed. Compiled .pyc embed ABSOLUTE SOURCE PATHS, i.e. a machine-path
# leak that a TEXT-only audit cannot see, because they are binary.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editor / OS noise
compile_commands.json
.DS_Store
